A||N||8||LemonSky||What's that screeching sound from my trunk?||||5||
Z||000000||LemonSky||09-15-2000||11:01 PM||||Hello, everyone. For some reason, at odd times when I'm driving my '86 SE6, I'll hear a sudden screeching sound emanating from my engine area. It'll last only about five seconds, then cease. I think it's probably a worn belt, but being the automotive neophyte (hey, at least I fixed my e-brake) I'm not sure.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-15-2000||11:27 PM||||So that's where jimmy hoffa went.<P><BR>check the alternator waterpump and AC compressor if you have that. It could just be the belt but many times when it starts doing things like that there is a bearing binding.<P>If the AC is on when this happens turn it off and see if it stops. When the A6 compressor clutch cycles it can really slam the belt. If it stops when the AC is off then likely the belt is shot.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-16-2000||01:22 PM||||Here's a pure guess...<BR>There is a cooling blower back there, hiding in a little nook under the trunk.  It blows air onto the coil and alternator.  You can see the tubes which convey the air, between aft side of engine and rear firewall.<P>If it squalls intermittently like a heater blower does sometimes, maybe it needs service.  The blower runs whenever the radiator fan runs - which includes whenever the A/C is on.<P>Never messed with mine, so don't know if these blowers ever have problems.  It's just a thought, FWIW.<P>    <BR> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000003||EdsB52||09-16-2000||09:57 PM||||Ya, that alternator fan and ducting are there for a good reason. I was driving at about eighty-ninety a few months ago and heard this huge screeeeeetch from the rear, looked in my mirror and saw black smoke billowing out from the vents. It lasted about five seconds, so I slowed and kept driving. Soon the engine temp rose and I pulled over. The alternator had frozen up and obviously the belt got smoked. Pretty cool effects, but pretty screwed I was as I begged a ride home!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||09-16-2000||10:28 PM||||I can't help you with your problem but I think I found the source of the squeaking sounds from my front compartment.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mousemotor.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Conrad Sanville||09-17-2000||08:25 PM||||I had an intermittent screech in the engine compartment on my 86 GT.  I narrowed it down to the air intake.  Turns out the air filter was in need of replacement. You might want to check that.  I hope that's your problem! <P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
Z||000006||Conrad Sanville||09-17-2000||08:25 PM||||I had an intermittent screech in the engine compartment on my 86 GT.  I narrowed it down to the air intake.  Turns out the air filter was in need of replacement. You might want to check that.  I hope that's your problem! <P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fearless Freep||09-17-2000||08:41 PM||||hey Phil....is that a NOS tank on his back?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||09-18-2000||07:24 AM||||Sure is -Nitrous Mouse Motor||||reg||1
